WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.288
Here are the 5 key factors to consider for a successful wedding-parent makeup booking.

2
00:00:09.624 --> 00:00:13.152
1) Expertise: is it a wedding-parent specialist?

3
00:00:13.488 --> 00:00:18.096
The first thing to check is whether the shop specializes in wedding parents, not brides.

4
00:00:18.432 --> 00:00:22.848
Large wedding shops put their veteran staff on the bride,

5
00:00:23.184 --> 00:00:28.176
and often leave the parents to weekend part-timers — an assembly-line system.

6
00:00:28.512 --> 00:00:34.944
Wedding-parent makeup has to address middle-age concerns like drooping eyelids, nasolabial folds, and thinning hair at the crown,

7
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:41.256
so be sure a specialist with real hands-on experience and an understanding of bone structure handles it personally.

8
00:00:41.592 --> 00:00:45.624
2) Logistics: visiting the shop vs. on-site makeup.

9
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:48.888
How you get there shapes how you feel on the day.

10
00:00:49.224 --> 00:00:53.232
Visiting the shop means full facilities and equipment,

11
00:00:53.568 --> 00:00:56.976
but there is the hassle of travel and the risk of traffic.

12
00:00:57.312 --> 00:01:03.504
On-site makeup, by contrast, lets you get ready comfortably at home or a hotel, saving time and energy.

13
00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:09.480
If you go on-site, make sure the business is properly licensed,

14
00:01:09.816 --> 00:01:13.824
so you avoid no-shows or subpar work.

15
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.400
3) Price: what counts as reasonable.

16
00:01:17.736 --> 00:01:22.680
In Seoul, a fair range for wedding-parent makeup is about 200,000–300,000 won.

17
00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:29.664
Shops under 100,000 won often assign a junior trainee, or charge separately for wigs, false lashes, and hair fiber powder,

18
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.272
which pushes the final price up — be careful.

19
00:01:34.608 --> 00:01:41.472
Prioritizing skilled technique and dedicated one-on-one service over price is the secret to a choice you won't regret.

20
00:01:41.808 --> 00:01:45.792
4) Separate spaces: a private, comfortable setting.

21
00:01:46.128 --> 00:01:50.088
Parents are very nervous and sensitive on the wedding day.

22
00:01:50.424 --> 00:01:55.656
To spare you the awkwardness of meeting your child's in-laws bare-faced, and to keep the parents at ease,

23
00:01:55.992 --> 00:02:00.624
look for a place with its own separate private rooms.

24
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:08.856
A quiet, unhurried setting steadies the parents emotionally, and that shows up as a warm smile and confidence at the ceremony.

25
00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:13.752
5) Kindness and attentive care: the one-on-one pre-consultation.

26
00:02:14.088 --> 00:02:19.080
Wedding-parent makeup should be more than technique — it should look after the parents' feelings.

27
00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:23.880
Be sure to check whether they offer a one-on-one consultation before booking.

28
00:02:24.216 --> 00:02:33.840
Meeting a specialist in advance to share concerns and settle on a style turns the day's anxiety into confidence, letting the parents feel like the stars they are.

29
00:02:34.176 --> 00:02:37.560
A well-prepared parent is the most confident and beautiful.

30
00:02:37.896 --> 00:02:40.368
Compare these factors carefully.
